# Workstation tool index (Template)

> ⚠️ **This is a template. The real `tool-index.md` is auto-generated by scripts and gitignored (machine-specific).**

---

## First run

Run one of the following to generate your workstation tool index:

```powershell
# Windows (PowerShell)
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "skills/scripts/refresh-tool-index.ps1"
```

```bash
# Linux / macOS / Kali
bash skills/scripts/refresh-tool-index.sh
```

---

## Generated format

Windows (PowerShell) produces an 8-column table:
| Tool | Owning skill | Purpose | Available | Path | Version | Source | Script reference |

Linux/macOS (Bash) produces a 7-column table:
| Tool | Skill | Purpose | Available | Path | Version | Install hint |

Both also append a "Capability Status" sub-table with MCP registration state and live service probes.

